  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_2",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_2",
  "label": "User projected onto the visual interaction scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the scene of the woman questioning the child. The visual material of the woman looking down at the child, combined with the rhetorical question, invites the user to project themselves into the role of the observer or judge of the interaction. The user is not explicitly addressed in the visual material, but the rhetorical question in the text directs the user's attention to the woman, making the user feel as if they are the one asking the question or evaluating the situation. This projection is onto the scene, which includes both the woman and the child, and the user is invited to see themselves as the moral authority in this context.",
